WEBVTT

00:00:19.000 --> 00:00:23.160
people public shelter an enemy attack has just occurred

00:00:23.160 --> 00:00:29.960
the first hours of shelter occupation are characterized by confusion rumors

00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:36.180
noise. Small groups gather. They discuss their situation, their new and strange location.

00:00:37.450 --> 00:00:43.660
This, however, is not the case with all shelter occupants. Some withdraw, freeze, become a member

00:00:43.660 --> 00:00:50.650
of no group. But there is one common value, one pervading thought, self-preservation,

00:00:51.420 --> 00:00:59.100
self-protection, self. Social values must return before individuals will function as a group.

00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:07.800
Luckily, the needs to achieve this are few: organization, leadership, recreation, training,

00:01:07.800 --> 00:01:14.510
empathy with fellow shelter occupants, but these needs are led by the need for information.

00:01:14.510 --> 00:01:19.910
The quality of the shelter's information program will have a great effect on the success

00:01:19.910 --> 00:01:30.000
of the survival effort. Your attention, please. Your attention, please. All right, quiet.

00:01:30.120 --> 00:01:41.460
This is Governor Haynes. This is an official announcement. The nation has sustained a nuclear attack.

00:01:42.140 --> 00:01:47.700
Luckily, only a few of our cities have been hit, and our citizens are now entering into shelters.

00:01:47.700 --> 00:01:55.770
If we stay in our shelters, we will survive. Your local authorities will give you reports as they are received.

00:01:56.370 --> 00:01:59.440
In the meantime, remember, stay in your shelter.

00:02:00.990 --> 00:02:06.610
positive information is reassuring. To get it, a radio is desirable. Providing shelters

00:02:06.610 --> 00:02:12.790
with radios is the responsibility of the community. But although it gives the big picture, the

00:02:12.790 --> 00:02:19.260
radio is an impersonal thing. What about our town, our neighborhood, our home?

00:02:19.260 --> 00:02:29.730
Ladies and gentlemen, may I have your attention for just a moment? You've heard our governor

00:02:30.190 --> 00:02:33.630
We have other information that there's been no heavy damage in our area.

00:02:34.380 --> 00:02:37.700
So if some of your family is not in this shelter, be reassured.

00:02:38.530 --> 00:02:40.210
Fill out these registration forms.

00:02:40.290 --> 00:02:41.610
It'll help us to locate your families.

00:02:42.050 --> 00:02:42.530
That's all.

00:02:50.750 --> 00:02:54.870
Evidence of informed leadership helps to establish control of the shelter quickly

00:02:54.870 --> 00:02:56.030
and to hold it.

00:02:56.030 --> 00:03:00.000
A major source of information.

00:03:00.000 --> 00:03:02.420
for management is the control center.

00:03:03.340 --> 00:03:05.080
The control center provides the manager

00:03:05.080 --> 00:03:07.840
with operations information not given over the radio.

00:03:08.750 --> 00:03:10.310
Some of this operations information

00:03:10.310 --> 00:03:12.830
may also be used as general information

00:03:12.830 --> 00:03:14.850
to further inform the shelter occupants

00:03:14.850 --> 00:03:16.750
at the discretion of the manager.

00:03:18.110 --> 00:03:20.130
Because information is so important,

00:03:20.800 --> 00:03:22.420
the shelter's procedure for handling it

00:03:22.420 --> 00:03:25.040
should be organized in an information program

00:03:25.040 --> 00:03:27.960
and made a part of the shelter operations plan.

00:03:28.660 --> 00:03:30.000
It should contain instructions

00:03:30.090 --> 00:03:32.490
to help others conduct the information program

00:03:32.490 --> 00:03:34.190
even if the manager and his staff

00:03:34.190 --> 00:03:36.750
don't make it to their shelter.

00:03:36.750 --> 00:03:39.650
The information program requires capable personnel

00:03:39.650 --> 00:03:41.820
to form an information team.

00:03:41.820 --> 00:03:45.220
Its leader could be a newsman or public relations expert,

00:03:45.220 --> 00:03:46.950
an educator or the like.

00:03:46.950 --> 00:03:49.250
The number and qualifications of his assistants

00:03:49.250 --> 00:03:52.090
will vary with the size and layout of the shelter.

00:03:52.090 --> 00:03:56.750
All should be chosen for their understanding of people.

00:03:56.750 --> 00:03:59.380
Once he feels safe in a well-managed shelter,

00:04:00.000 --> 00:04:05.280
Shelter occupants' concern for self quickly gives way to concern about his immediate family.

00:04:05.960 --> 00:04:09.800
The information team should be prepared to cope with this demanding need.

00:04:12.370 --> 00:04:20.990
We're in contact with Control Center downtown.

00:04:22.540 --> 00:04:27.420
They report that all shelters in Fairview have been occupied according to plan.

00:04:29.090 --> 00:04:30.000
All children have gone.

00:04:30.000 --> 00:04:36.820
gone safely into their school shelters. They urge that we stay in our shelter.

00:04:36.820 --> 00:04:44.800
Reassuring news about family can help draw distraught individuals out of

00:04:44.800 --> 00:04:49.660
themselves. Supplying information helps them start back to a normal condition of

00:04:49.660 --> 00:04:54.630
social awareness and responsibility. They will form spontaneous groups to talk out

00:04:54.630 --> 00:04:59.880
the situation, relieving pressure. But these groups lack purpose and organization.

00:05:00.350 --> 00:05:07.040
They must be given more information to help management build a close-knit shelter society for survival.

00:05:07.040 --> 00:05:12.520
As soon as possible, post a public announcement schedule.

00:05:12.520 --> 00:05:17.950
List the times that you intend to announce news from both outside and inside the shelter.

00:05:17.950 --> 00:05:20.730
This is similar to regular newscasts.

00:05:20.730 --> 00:05:24.490
It will give shelter occupants regular high points to look forward to.

00:05:24.490 --> 00:05:30.000
Urgent announcements, of course, should be made immediately, just as in normal times.

00:05:30.410 --> 00:05:35.600
issuing the news is a critical responsibility of trust the timely release of

00:05:35.600 --> 00:05:40.070
news and the preparation of the occupants to accept bad news when

00:05:40.070 --> 00:05:45.350
necessary are the responsibility of the shelter manager and his staff your

00:05:45.350 --> 00:05:51.260
attention please your attention please as we expected fallout is moving over

00:05:51.260 --> 00:05:56.750
the city radiation levels have not been determined as yet another information

00:05:56.750 --> 00:05:59.760
problem concerns the issuance of bad news

00:06:00.480 --> 00:06:04.120
The public has as much right to know the unpleasant as the cheerful.

00:06:04.970 --> 00:06:08.950
Knowing just how to deliver it and how to cope with possible reaction

00:06:08.950 --> 00:06:12.290
is the essence of a good information program.

00:06:12.290 --> 00:06:16.810
If the manager believes that the effect on morale is serious,

00:06:17.290 --> 00:06:22.670
he must be prepared to offset this with positive instructions and information.

00:06:24.060 --> 00:06:30.000
The manner in which information is given is extremely important, calmly rather than excitedly.

00:06:30.670 --> 00:06:37.140
authoritative rather than confused. Giving both good news and bad, keeping shelter occupants

00:06:37.140 --> 00:06:44.320
informed of outside events, asking for ideas, confiding serious problems, will gradually

00:06:44.320 --> 00:06:51.750
draw individuals into a group with a growing morale and a willingness to cooperate.

00:06:51.750 --> 00:06:56.830
But as the group spirit develops, there will be ever-present forces that tend to divide

00:06:56.830 --> 00:07:00.000
it again. One of these is a familiar information problem.

00:07:06.460 --> 00:07:10.530
round. Some of them want to sleep in the other half of the room tonight because they say there's less

00:07:10.530 --> 00:07:15.340
radiation over there. Well, that figures. All of them tried to sleep over here last night.

00:07:15.730 --> 00:07:19.230
The rumor then was that only this end of the shelter was safe. The rumors are canceling

00:07:19.230 --> 00:07:23.990
each other out. All right, let's have Charlie set up a demonstration to prove that both rumors

00:07:23.990 --> 00:07:28.060
are just scuttlebutt. When they have the correct information, we won't have a problem.

00:07:34.000 --> 00:07:40.790
After some time, there will be opportunities to use the program and communications facilities to help improve morale.

00:07:40.790 --> 00:07:45.920
There may be time to transmit information that will have a personal meaning to shelter occupants,

00:07:45.920 --> 00:07:49.920
perhaps to confirm the good health of family members who are in other shelters.

00:07:49.920 --> 00:07:56.140
Important morale-boosting information of this sort should be compiled and transmitted during the slack hours

00:07:56.140 --> 00:08:00.000
to avoid confusing or delaying important official operations.

00:08:00.000 --> 00:08:01.100
and general messages.

00:08:01.950 --> 00:08:03.470
Another information technique

00:08:03.470 --> 00:08:05.590
that helps increase the group spirit

00:08:05.590 --> 00:08:07.590
is to share personal news

00:08:07.590 --> 00:08:08.490
with the whole shelter.

00:08:09.150 --> 00:08:10.770
There will be many opportunities.

00:08:12.600 --> 00:08:14.380
Well, that about wraps it up for now.

00:08:15.810 --> 00:08:17.870
If there's anyone who has anything that he'd like,

00:08:23.860 --> 00:08:26.140
well, looks like we do have

00:08:26.140 --> 00:08:27.300
another bit of news.

00:08:31.340 --> 00:08:35.960
The Webbers have an anniversary today, they're 30th.

00:08:35.960 --> 00:08:45.160
Congratulations!

00:08:45.160 --> 00:08:49.580
When the routine of existence has at last been established in the shelter, and news

00:08:49.580 --> 00:08:53.240
becomes repetitious, life may become boring.

00:08:53.240 --> 00:08:56.550
Shelter occupants will ask, "What do we do now?"

00:08:56.550 --> 00:09:00.000
The information program should include ways to help solve the problem.

00:09:00.670 --> 00:09:04.920
It's comparatively easy to handle an individual, give them responsibilities.

00:09:05.580 --> 00:09:11.850
But for the group as a whole, the answer is organized instruction to further inform and

00:09:11.850 --> 00:09:13.410
orient the shelter occupants.

00:09:13.410 --> 00:09:20.020
The program should include talks on preserving health, discussion periods, safety instruction,

00:09:20.740 --> 00:09:26.360
special activities for adults and children, and other activities that underscore the need

00:09:26.360 --> 00:09:30.000
for tolerance, cooperation, and submergence of parents.

00:09:30.000 --> 00:09:35.910
personal interest for the good of the group. If possible, personnel needed to direct these

00:09:35.910 --> 00:09:41.060
activities should be designated pre-attack from the community ranks of trained specialists.

00:09:41.060 --> 00:09:46.470
If more are required, they can be selected with the help of the registration forms

00:09:46.470 --> 00:09:51.440
from among the shelter occupants, school teachers, recreation and athletic directors,

00:09:51.940 --> 00:10:00.000
professional people and church leaders. The total effect of their

00:10:00.000 --> 00:10:05.550
instruction should be to improve shelter life and to prepare survivors for the

00:10:05.550 --> 00:10:10.850
post-shelter world. This indeed will be an important part of the information

00:10:10.850 --> 00:10:16.460
program preparing for the post-shelter world. On those who survive will fall a

00:10:16.460 --> 00:10:22.250
great responsibility re-establishing a normal way of life. How well that is

00:10:22.250 --> 00:10:25.060
achieved will be influenced by the quality of

00:10:25.060 --> 00:10:30.000
instruction provided in public shelters. So in brief, the shelter in

00:10:30.000 --> 00:10:35.910
information program, informs, diverts, and orients shelter occupants during the

00:10:35.910 --> 00:10:40.750
long days of confinement. It produces what is vital to shelter functioning and

00:10:40.750 --> 00:10:47.770
management: an informed population. And it does something more.

00:10:47.770 --> 00:10:57.840
Thank you, Doctor.

00:11:00.800 --> 00:11:06.940
And now, finally, to the matter that we've all been thinking about, just when can we

00:11:06.940 --> 00:11:15.370
all leave the shelter? It has been several days. Radiation fallout has decayed, but

00:11:15.370 --> 00:11:20.370
there still is some radiation present. So as you know, the staff does not believe that

00:11:20.370 --> 00:11:30.000
anyone should go out. Some of you do. Now again, you realize that we don't want to hold anyone in the

00:11:30.000 --> 00:11:37.070
shelter against his will. So before you make your final decision, it might be wise to hear

00:11:37.070 --> 00:11:46.100
how some of the others feel. Can I say something? Yes, of course, Mr. Mills. Go ahead. Well,

00:11:46.100 --> 00:11:51.370
I only got on the information team pretty recently. To be honest with all of you, maybe

00:11:51.370 --> 00:12:00.000
I just got on any team pretty recently. What I mean is, when I got here right after, I was kind

00:12:01.470 --> 00:12:02.450
I guess we all were.

00:12:03.930 --> 00:12:06.180
Didn't know what was happening.

00:12:06.300 --> 00:12:07.380
I felt closed in.

00:12:07.790 --> 00:12:11.110
I know none of us did at first, but it really got to me.

00:12:11.990 --> 00:12:14.220
Sure helped finding out about the kids, though.

00:12:14.600 --> 00:12:15.990
I got a couple myself.

00:12:16.510 --> 00:12:18.330
And the things were being taken care of.

00:12:19.750 --> 00:12:23.590
What I really want to say is I want to go along with whatever these people,

00:12:23.850 --> 00:12:25.540
the manager and the staff, say.

00:12:26.190 --> 00:12:28.110
We can make a big mistake by going out there.

00:12:28.110 --> 00:12:29.880
Here is the something extra.

00:12:30.410 --> 00:12:33.430
that a good information program gives.

00:12:33.430 --> 00:12:37.140
It helps replace self-concern and disorientation

00:12:37.140 --> 00:12:40.620
with concern for others, interest in the group,

00:12:40.620 --> 00:12:42.330
responsibility.

00:12:42.330 --> 00:12:46.250
More than individuals will survive in the fallout shelter.

00:12:46.250 --> 00:12:50.900
With a good program, society will survive too.
